  "question": {
    "text": "Consider a thermodynamic process where internal energy $U=A P^2 \\mathrm{~V}(\\mathrm{~A}=$ constant). If the process is performed adiabatically, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "EYOdG",
      "text": "$A P^2(V+1)=$ constant",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JXVaj",
      "text": "$(\\mathrm{AP}+1)^2 \\mathrm{~V}=\\mathrm{constant}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "azkld",
      "text": "$(\\mathrm{AP}+1) \\mathrm{V}^2=$ constant",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pmxGr",
      "text": "$\\frac{V}{(A P+1)^2}=$ constant",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$U=A P^2 V$\n$\\frac{d U}{d V}=A P^2+2 P A V \\frac{d P}{d V}$ [For adiabatic process $\\left.d Q=0, d U=-d w=-P d V\\right]$\n$-\\frac{P d V}{d V}=A P^2+2 P A V \\frac{d P}{d V}$\n$-1=A P+2 A V \\frac{d P}{d V} \\Rightarrow-1-A P=2 A V \\frac{d P}{d V}$\n$-\\int \\frac{d V}{V}=\\int \\frac{2 A d P}{A P+1}$\n$-\\ell n V+C=\\frac{2 A}{A} \\ln (A P+1)$\n$C=\\ell n(A P+1)^2+\\ell n V \\Rightarrow C=(A P+1)^2 V$",
    "image": null
  },
